  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 6.5,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 6.5,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-22: the record charged a 6.50 SGD no-show fee against the fixed 5.00 SGD fee (EV-FARE-05060, fee_matches_policy false). The ruling acts on the amount charged, and the 1.50 SGD discrepancy is referred to the platform under this clause."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this ruling is for the driver, who filed it. The rider no-show was valid, so the 6.50 SGD taken back from the driver is returned to him as compensation.\n\nNo-show preconditions (POL-NS-21, POL-NS-23). The driver marked arrival at 14:09:15 and the GPS trace corroborates it: the nearest fix at 14:09:55 sits 2.89 m from the pickup at a reported accuracy of 4.0 m, inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius and the 25 m accuracy filter, on a 25-fix, 100%-coverage trace with no gap over 30 s. The 300 s free wait ran from arrival and expired at 14:14:15; the driver cancelled at 14:15:40, 385 s after arrival and 85 s after expiry. Before cancelling he sent in-app messages at 14:09:40 and 14:13:00 and placed an in-app call at 14:12:10. Both limbs of the driver's contact obligation are therefore met, so POL-NS-23 supplies no full refund. The driver's claims on these points, and the rider's concession of them, are accepted.\n\nAmount (POL-NS-22). The policy fee is 5.00 SGD, but the record charged 6.50 SGD (EV-FARE-05060; fee_matches_policy false), and POL-NS-22 says that where the record charged an amount other than 5.00 SGD the ruling acts on the amount charged and adds a referral. The driver's compensation is therefore 6.50 SGD. The rider's argument that only 5.00 SGD can be paid, so that the driver's claim fails as filed and NO_ACTION follows, is rejected: the 1.50 SGD excess is dealt with by the POL-NS-22 referral, not by cutting the driver's entitlement. The rider keeps the 6.50 SGD already refunded to him; the ruling does not re-charge him.\n\nEscalation arguments (POL-NS-24, POL-GEN-26, POL-GEN-02). The rider argues that the absence of a scheduled pickup time (EV-TRIP-05060, driver_deadline null, on-demand trip) leaves a needed fact unestablished and requires human review. Rejected: POL-NS-24's driver-late test is not engaged here (the rider did not cancel, the driver's arrival is independently corroborated, and no rule this ruling needs turns on a scheduled time), so POL-GEN-26's precondition is not met. The missing TRAFFIC_ADVISORY (EV-ADVIS-05060-01, status MISSING, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0) carries no fact under POL-GEN-02(3) and no no-show rule requires it, so it too supports no escalation.\n\nFinality and referral (POL-GEN-22, POL-NS-26, POL-NS-25). The dispute value is 6.50 SGD, below the 10.00 SGD AI-final threshold, and fraud_flags is 0 on both profiles, so this ruling is final. POL-NS-25 is not engaged: the rider profile carries no no_show_cancellations_30d counter, so no repeat-no-show flag is added. The only referral is POL-NS-22's fee-amount check.\n\nThe rider's counter-statement does not deny the no-show; it questions only the amount, which the referral answers. Figures used: fee charged 6.50 SGD; policy fee 5.00 SGD; refund already issued to the rider 6.50 SGD."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
